<LegalLayout title="Privacy Policy - Back Pain Log" description="Privacy Policy for the Back Pain Log iOS app.">
  <p class="eyebrow">Back Pain Log</p>
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="effective">Effective date: 19 August 2026</p>

  <p>Back Pain Log is designed to be private and offline.</p>

  <h2>Data collection</h2>
  <p>Back Pain Log does not collect data from you. There are no accounts, no analytics, no advertising trackers, and no developer server receiving your app data.</p>

  <h2>Local storage</h2>
  <p>Your discomfort logs, treatment selections, notes, favourites, treatment order, and reminder preference are stored locally on your device. The app does not use a network connection to send this information to us.</p>

  <h2>CSV export</h2>
  <p>Back Pain Log includes a CSV export feature. Export is started by you. Once exported, you choose where to save or share the file, for example with a physio, GP, or your own records. We do not receive exported files unless you deliberately send them to us.</p>

  <h2>Daily reminders</h2>
  <p>If you enable a daily reminder, it is scheduled on your device. We do not receive reminder data.</p>

  <h2>Medical note</h2>
  <p>Back Pain Log is a diary, not medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment. If pain is severe, changing, or worrying, consider speaking with a qualified health professional.</p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>If this policy changes, we will update the effective date above and post the revised policy at this address.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>If you have questions about this privacy policy, contact <a href="mailto:support@mikhailnarbekov.com">support@mikhailnarbekov.com</a>.</p>
</LegalLayout>
